From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 12:16:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0158 -- wave-62 textbox FT=1 state/draw
 split (4-way)

Under SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FIXED_TIMESTEP (patch 0153, wave-57) the
accumulator multi-runs Game::tick_state() N times per displayed frame
while tick_render_submit() / flip() run once. For that to be correct,
everything tick_state() reaches must be drawcall-free game-state work
-- the wave-36 trap is putting drawcalls in the multi-run path.

The textbox subsystem advanced its state inside game_tick_normal_render
via textbox.Tick() (game.cpp:859), i.e. at the render rate. Under FT=1
that desyncs the textbox from the 50 Hz logic clock: text scroll-in and
the yes/no / stage-select / save-select prompt state machines tick at
whatever the display manages, not the fixed rate the rest of the sim
runs at.

This splits the textbox state from its draw so the state half can move
into tick_state. TextBox::Tick() interleaves a trailing Draw(), and so
do all three menu sub-Ticks (TB_YNJPrompt / TB_StageSelect /
TB_SaveSelect each end with Draw()) -- so a single split is not enough;
moving TextBox::Tick() wholesale into tick_state would pull three sub-
prompt Draw() calls into the multi-run path. Hence a 4-way split: each
of the 4 classes gains a drawcall-free TickState() (its state work with
the trailing Draw() removed). TextBox::TickState() calls the 3 sub-
TickState()s + TickTextBox.

FT=0 byte-identity: TextBox::Tick(), TB_StageSelect::Tick() and
TB_SaveSelect::Tick() are left verbatim -- the FT=0 path and the title /
inventory callers keep calling them unchanged. TextBox::Tick() MUST
stay verbatim specifically: it calls each sub-prompt's .Tick() (which
draws) AND TextBox::Draw() draws them again, so each sub-prompt is
drawn twice per frame -- and TB_StageSelect::Draw() / TB_SaveSelect::
Draw() are NOT idempotent (they mutate fWarpY / fPicXOffset, the menu
slide-in animations). De-dupping TextBox::Tick() would drop one draw
and halve those animation rates -- an FT=0 render difference. So only
TB_YNJPrompt::Tick() is reduced to { TickState(); Draw(); }: its Draw()
is pure drawSprite calls (idempotent), and its Tick() still calls
Draw() exactly once itself, so the reduction is behavior-identical and
removes the otherwise-duplicated ~33-line YN state machine. TickState()
is new code invoked only on the FT=1 path.

FT=1 wiring: Game::tick_state() calls textbox.TickState() alongside the
wave-57 screen-effect Tick relocations, gated to TD_GM_NORMAL_SPLIT so
it runs only on GM_NORMAL ticks (paused / mode-transition ticks skip
it, as the render-half textbox.Tick() would not have run; other modes
tick the textbox via their own unchanged Tick() calls). The
game.cpp:859 site becomes FT-gated: textbox.Draw() on FT=1 (state
already advanced in tick_state -- a textbox.Tick() there would tick the
state twice per frame), textbox.Tick() unchanged on FT=0.

On FT=1 the sub-prompts are drawn once (via TextBox::Draw) instead of
twice; YNJPrompt draw is idempotent, and the StageSelect warp-text /
SaveSelect pic-slide run at 1x instead of 2x -- a known minor FT=1-only
cosmetic delta (FT=1 is not byte-identity-gated), deferred per the
wave-62 contract rather than fixed in-wave.

The YNJPrompt accept-consume (lastinputs[ACCEPT_BUTTON] /
lastpinputs[ACCEPT_BUTTON] writes) is multi-run-safe: run_tick_fixed
re-snapshots lastinputs[] at the start of every catch-up iteration so
justpushed() edges de-dup, and SetVisible(false) on accept makes
iterations 2..N early-return. No new env var (reuses FIXED_TIMESTEP).

