+// DOS-PORT (patch 0158, Phase 11 wave-62): Tick() is now a pure
+// { TickState(); Draw(); }. The YN state machine lives ONLY in
+// TickState() below -- no duplicate copy. This is behavior-identical to
+// the pre-0158 switch-then-Draw() Tick(): Tick() still runs the state
+// machine once (via TickState) and calls Draw() exactly once itself, so
+// FT=0 is byte-identical. (TextBox::Tick() / StageSelect::Tick() /
+// SaveSelect::Tick() are left verbatim -- de-dupping TextBox::Tick()
+// would drop one of the two per-frame sub-prompt Draw() calls, and
+// StageSelect/SaveSelect Draw() are non-idempotent: G2-unsafe. Only
+// YNJPrompt is de-dupped here because only its Tick() had an inline
+// duplicate and only its Draw() is pure / idempotent.)
 void TB_YNJPrompt::Tick()
+{
+  TickState();
+  Draw();
+}
+
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0158, Phase 11 wave-62): the drawcall-free state half
+// of Tick() -- holds the YN state machine (the sole copy; Tick() above
+// is { TickState(); Draw(); }). The render half draws via
+// TextBox::Draw() -> YesNoPrompt.Draw(). Multi-run-safe under
+// FIXED_TIMESTEP: run_tick_fixed re-snapshots lastinputs[] each catch-up
